course: dictionary
lesson: 2299
title: Crinkly: folds and crackles
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how something looks, and some tell you how it sounds. Crinkly can do both. In «His proud paws go crinkly, he loses the soap for the fiftieth time», crinkly means the paws have lots of small folds and lines, like skin that has been soaking in water for a long time.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. He is still trying to wash something, his back aches, and he has dropped the soap fifty times. These words show he is tired and frustrated, and they describe his paws, not a noise. So the folds meaning fits here.
explain: Crinkly has a second meaning too: it makes a light crackling sound when you touch or crush it, like crisp paper or foil. To check which meaning fits, put it into the sentence and ask: does it make sense? Do the paws crackle when they are touched? No, so the folds meaning is right.
fact: Crinkly means having lots of small folds, lines or wrinkles.
fact: Crinkly also means making a light crackling sound when touched or crushed.
fact: Crinkly is an adjective, and its forms are crinkly, crinklier and crinkliest.
fact: Things can be crinkly in the ways you see, like smiling eyes or crinkly leaves, or in the ways you hear, like crinkly paper or crinkly crisps.
fact: Crinkly is also used for hair, as in crinkly hair.
exercise: «His proud paws go crinkly.» What does crinkly mean here? | Making a loud bang | Cold and hard | *Covered in lots of small folds and wrinkles | Shiny and smooth
exercise: Which thing is crinkly because it makes a crackling sound when crushed? | *Crisp packet | Sleeping cat | Glass window | Wooden table
exercise: «The old man smiled, and his eyes went ___ at the edges.» Which word fits the gap? | sharp | hollow | silent | *crinkly
test: «Dad's face was ___ when he laughed, with little lines around his eyes.» Which word fits the gap? | Silent | *Crinkly | Furious | Sharp
test: What does crinkly mean in «crinkly foil»? | *Full of folds that crackle when crushed | Frozen solid | Shiny and new | Very heavy
exam: Which sentence uses crinkly to mean making a crackling sound? | «Her crinkly eyes twinkled when she smiled.» | *«He crumpled the crinkly foil and it crackled.» | «The crinkly soup was hot.» | «Grandad's crinkly hair was grey.»
